.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/@nodelib/fs.stat Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "@nodelib/fs\&.stat"
.PP
.RS 4
Get the status of a file with some features\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SH ":bulb: Highlights"
.PP
Wrapper around standard method \fRfs\&.lstat\fP and \fRfs\&.stat\fP with some features\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
:beginner: Normally follows symbolic link\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
:gear: Can safely work with broken symbolic link\&.
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install @nodelib/fs\&.stat
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
import * as fsStat from '@nodelib/fs\&.stat';

fsStat\&.stat('path', (error, stats) => { /* … */ });
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "\&.stat(path, [optionsOrSettings], callback)"
Returns an instance of \fRfs\&.Stats\fP class for provided path with standard callback-style\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
fsStat\&.stat('path', (error, stats) => { /* … */ });
fsStat\&.stat('path', {}, (error, stats) => { /* … */ });
fsStat\&.stat('path', new fsStat\&.Settings(), (error, stats) => { /* … */ });
.fi
.PP
.SS "\&.statSync(path, [optionsOrSettings])"
Returns an instance of \fRfs\&.Stats\fP class for provided path\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const stats = fsStat\&.stat('path');
const stats = fsStat\&.stat('path', {});
const stats = fsStat\&.stat('path', new fsStat\&.Settings());
.fi
.PP
.SS "path"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Required: \fRtrue\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRstring | Buffer | URL\fP
.PP

.PP
A path to a file\&. If a URL is provided, it must use the \fRfile:\fP protocol\&.
.SS "optionsOrSettings"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Required: \fRfalse\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fROptions | Settings\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: An instance of \fRSettings\fP class
.PP

.PP
An \fB`Options`\fP object or an instance of \fB`Settings`\fP class\&.

.PP
.RS 4
:book: When you pass a plain object, an instance of the \fRSettings\fP class will be created automatically\&. If you plan to call the method frequently, use a pre-created instance of the \fRSettings\fP class\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SS "Settings([options])"
A class of full settings of the package\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const settings = new fsStat\&.Settings({ followSymbolicLink: false });

const stats = fsStat\&.stat('path', settings);
.fi
.PP
.SH "Options"
.PP
.SS "\fRfollowSymbolicLink\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRboolean\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRtrue\fP
.PP

.PP
Follow symbolic link or not\&. Call \fRfs\&.stat\fP on symbolic link if \fRtrue\fP\&.
.SS "\fRmarkSymbolicLink\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRboolean\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRfalse\fP
.PP

.PP
Mark symbolic link by setting the return value of \fRisSymbolicLink\fP function to always \fRtrue\fP (even after \fRfs\&.stat\fP)\&.

.PP
.RS 4
:book: Can be used if you want to know what is hidden behind a symbolic link, but still continue to know that it is a symbolic link\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SS "\fRthrowErrorOnBrokenSymbolicLink\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRboolean\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRtrue\fP
.PP

.PP
Throw an error when symbolic link is broken if \fRtrue\fP or safely return \fRlstat\fP call if \fRfalse\fP\&.
.SS "\fRfs\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fR\fRFileSystemAdapter\fP\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: A default FS methods
.PP

.PP
By default, the built-in Node\&.js module (\fRfs\fP) is used to work with the file system\&. You can replace any method with your own\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
interface FileSystemAdapter {
    lstat?: typeof fs\&.lstat;
    stat?: typeof fs\&.stat;
    lstatSync?: typeof fs\&.lstatSync;
    statSync?: typeof fs\&.statSync;
}

const settings = new fsStat\&.Settings({
    fs: { lstat: fakeLstat }
});
.fi
.PP
